content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Service Manager",
      "description": "person who oversees service performance and demand"
    },
    {
      "name": "Usage Data",
      "description": "data showing how users interact with the service"
    },
    {
      "name": "Demand Report",
      "description": "summary of expected or current demand trends"
    },
    {
      "name": "Fleet Coordinator",
      "description": "person who manages vehicle readiness and allocation"
    },
    {
      "name": "Fleet",
      "description": "collection of vehicles organized across zones",
      "attributes": [
        "Vehicle",
        "City Zone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "City Zone",
      "description": "area of operation within the service region"
    },
    {
      "name": "Vehicle",
      "description": "car available for booking",
      "attributes": [
        "Location"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Location",
      "description": "current geographic position of a vehicle"
    },
    {
      "name": "Cleaning Schedule",
      "description": "plan for when vehicles get cleaned"
    },
    {
      "name": "Fueling Schedule",
      "description": "plan for refueling vehicles"
    },
    {
      "name": "Customer Support Agent",
      "description": "person assisting users with issues and questions"
    },
    {
      "name": "Booking",
      "description": "user reservation for a vehicle",
      "attributes": [
        "Vehicle",
        "Price"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Price",
      "description": "cost associated with a booking"
    },
    {
      "name": "Pricing Strategy",
      "description": "rules that define how booking prices are set"
    },
    {
      "name": "Technical Assistance",
      "description": "help provided to users for technical or usage problems"
    },
    {
      "name": "Damage Report",
      "description": "record of issues or damage found on a vehicle",
      "attributes": [
        "Vehicle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "User",
      "description": "person booking and using vehicles",
      "attributes": [
        "Profile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "description": "stored personal and account details of a user"
    },
    {
      "name": "User Feedback",
      "description": "input from users about their ride experience"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Fleet Monitoring": {
      "objects": [
        "Fleet Coordinator",
        "Fleet",
        "City Zone",
        "Vehicle",
        "Location",
        "Cleaning Schedule",
        "Fueling Schedule"
      ]
    },
    "User Booking": {
      "objects": [
        "User",
        "Profile",
        "Booking",
        "Vehicle",
        "Price",
        "User Feedback",
        "Customer Support Agent",
        "Technical Assistance",
        "Damage Report"
      ]
    },
    "Administration": {
      "objects": [
        "Service Manager",
        "Usage Data",
        "Demand Report",
        "Pricing Strategy"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Administration--Fleet Monitoring",
      "User Booking--Fleet Monitoring",
      "Administration--User Booking"
    ]
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
